before:
```typescript
type Reading = { unit: string; amount: number };
type Amount = Reading["amount"];
function addOne(amount: Amount): Amount {
  return amount + 1;
}
console.log(addOne(4));
```
This prints 5. addOne takes Amount and returns Amount. Because Amount is number, amount + 1 is numeric addition. The brackets in the type alias operate on a type; the argument 4 supplies the runtime value. console.log displays the returned number.

```typescript
