  return amount + 1;
}
console.log(addOne(0));
```
This prints 1. Trace the changed value through the same rule.

after:
Amount reuses the field type in both the input and result.
```typescript
type Reading = { unit: string; amount: number };
type Amount = Reading["amount"];
function addOne(amount: Amount): Amount {
  return amount + 1;
}
console.log(addOne(4));
```
The output is 5.
